    "comment": {
      "comments": [
        {
          "id": "10000",
          "body": "**Starting Stage 1 development** (clickable Expo prototype, white-label wireframes).\n\nRead acceptance criteria from this ticket + epic [ROKJ-1](https://satsumya.atlassian.net/browse/ROKJ-1). Assumptions for prototype:\n\n* Email verification = mock screen (tap Continue)\n* Error handling = inline messages when fields empty\n* Sign up path: auth → verify email → welcome → [ROKJ-15](https://satsumya.atlassian.net/browse/ROKJ-15) profile → dashboard placeholder\n* Login path: auth → dashboard placeholder\n* No real auth/backend\n\nRepo: local `Rokjam` workspace. Will update this ticket as criteria are completed.",
          "created": "2026-06-20T14:01:30.964+1000",
          "updated": "2026-06-20T14:01:30.964+1000",
          "author": {
            "accountId": "712020:29c42df6-88fc-4646-aedc-3fdfa92e83a4",
            "displayName": "Sarah Barnes"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "10003",
          "body": "**Implementation complete — ready for review**\n\nAll acceptance criteria marked complete. Local Expo prototype covers sign up/login journeys per ticket.\n\n**Test paths:**\n\n1. Welcome → Sign up → (empty submit shows errors) → fill fields → Verify email → Welcome → Profile\n2. Welcome → Log in → (empty submit shows errors) → fill fields → Dashboard\n3. Toggle between sign up/login links on auth screens\n\n**Run locally:** `npm install && npm start`",
          "created": "2026-06-20T14:05:28.009+1000",
          "updated": "2026-06-20T14:05:28.009+1000",
          "author": {
            "accountId": "712020:29c42df6-88fc-4646-aedc-3fdfa92e83a4",
            "displayName": "Sarah Barnes"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "10005",
          "body": "Added prototype test links to the ticket description, populated the **Decision tree**, and reformatted **Outcome summary** as bullets + scenario table.\n\nAlso added `/scenarios` in the app — a scenario tester with one-click paths for happy / alternate / error flows.\n\nStart locally with `npm run web`, then open http://localhost:8081/scenarios",
          "created": "2026-06-20T14:15:16.196+1000",
          "updated": "2026-06-20T14:15:16.196+1000",
          "author": {
            "accountId": "712020:29c42df6-88fc-4646-aedc-3fdfa92e83a4",
            "displayName": "Sarah Barnes"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "10011",
          "body": "Review: <custom data-type=\"status\" data-id=\"id-0\">not approved</custom> \n\nPlease address the following:\n\n|  | **Summary** | **Description** |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | New user sign up default to blank input fields | New users would not have added any details please leave everything that would be expected to be blank as blank |\n| 2 | Input errors | Error validation should happen in real time instead of waiting until the user tries to continue |\n| 3 | Password standards | Add standards for passwords e.g. use at least one symbol etc |\n| 4 | Verification code | Let’s have users enter a code instead of clicking a link in an email. For testing purposes please make code: 000000 an error and every other number combination successfully verify |\n| 5 | Verification resend | If a user hasn’t received the code we’ll need a way for them to re-send the email or go back to try a different email |\n| 6 | Scenario for existing user attempts to sign up instead of login | If an email is recognised for an existing user and they try and sign up we could just log them in or redirect them to login |\n| 7 | Remove excess prototype text | Some text on this ticket was added for context but not needed on the prototype e.g. “Returning user enters details and lands on the dashboard.” Please remove any text that a user wouldn’t expect to see |\n| 8 | Sign up welcome screen | Needs an option to close. If they don’t want to jump straight into the member profile take them to the dashboard. Dashboard should then show prompts to create member profile or directly add some details from the dashboard |\n| 9 | Login with username or email | Ensure existing users can use their username or email in the input field |\n| 10 | Email validation | If a user enters an email that isn’t valid e.g. doesn’t have an '@' symbol they should see an error |\n| 11 | Password recovery for existing users | There needs to be an option to reset your password or recover your password |\n\nGeneral feedback: please use the existing ticket fields where possible e.g. decision tree and outcome summary. I’ve moved these from comments to the ticket fields",
          "created": "2026-06-20T15:13:39.027+1000",
          "updated": "2026-06-20T15:26:22.371+1000",
          "author": {
            "accountId": "712020:29c42df6-88fc-4646-aedc-3fdfa92e83a4",
            "displayName": "Sarah Barnes"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "10015",
          "body": "**Status check:** Wireframe is ready for review from last session.\n\n* Status: Review\n* Acceptance criteria: all marked DONE\n* Decision tree + Outcome summary fields updated (review feedback from comments 10011 / 10013)\n* Test: http://localhost:8081/scenarios\n\nJira MCP re-authenticated this session — no code changes needed on this ticket.",
          "created": "2026-07-04T15:14:56.611+1000",
